[
    {
        "content": "<p>(Apologies for pushing send before a previous draft of this message was complete.)</p>\n<p>Suppose I'm in <code>MetaM</code> and want to look up the type of a given identifier (which might be defined locally or globally).  I can do this, which works:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Lean</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">open</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Lean</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Elab</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Term</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">open</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Lean</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Meta</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">z</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">7</span>\n\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">eval</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">do</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">e</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">elabTerm</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">`</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">z</span><span class=\"o\">))</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">none</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">inferType</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">e</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">pure</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"c1\">-- produces Lean.Expr.const `Nat []</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>But it feels slightly heavyweight to invoke the machinery of <code>elabTerm</code> here (and it also requires the <code>TermElabM</code> monad).  Is there some more efficient, lower-level way to perform this lookup?</p>",
        "id": 627421298,
        "sender_full_name": "Adam Dingle",
        "timestamp": 1790598563
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>You should be able to get the monad state and its <code>ConstMap</code>, which offers a lookup by name</p>",
        "id": 627431504,
        "sender_full_name": "Arthur Paulino",
        "timestamp": 1790600885
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>There are several ways depending on what you need:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Lean</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">open</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Lean</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Meta</span>\n\n<span class=\"sd\">/-- info: [u], {α : Sort u} → α → α -/</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">guard_msgs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span>\n<span class=\"n\">run_meta</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">val</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">getConstVal</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"ss\">``id</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">lparams</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">val</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">levelParams</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">type</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">val</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">type</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">logInfo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">m!</span><span class=\"s2\">\"{lparams}, {type}\"</span>\n\n<span class=\"sd\">/-- info: {α : Type} → α → α -/</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">guard_msgs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span>\n<span class=\"n\">run_meta</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">e</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">const</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"ss\">``id</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">inferType</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">e</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">logInfo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">m!</span><span class=\"s2\">\"{t}\"</span>\n\n<span class=\"sd\">/-- info: {α : Sort ?u.1} → α → α -/</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">guard_msgs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span>\n<span class=\"n\">run_meta</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">e</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">mkConstWithFreshMVarLevels</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"ss\">``id</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">inferType</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">e</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">logInfo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">m!</span><span class=\"s2\">\"{t}\"</span>\n\n<span class=\"sd\">/-- info: [?α, ?a], #[Lean.BinderInfo.implicit, Lean.BinderInfo.default], ?α -/</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">guard_msgs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span>\n<span class=\"n\">run_meta</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">e</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">mkConstWithFreshMVarLevels</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"ss\">``id</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">vars</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">bis</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">body</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">forallMetaTelescope</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">inferType</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">e</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">logInfo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">m!</span><span class=\"s2\">\"{vars}, {repr bis}, {body}\"</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 627434208,
        "sender_full_name": "Robin Arnez",
        "timestamp": 1790601462
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Lean.getConstVal#doc\">docs#Lean.getConstVal</a> is the primitive that everything is based on. It gives you the level parameters along with the type which you can use as the level parameters of a new declaration if you want to make a new declaration based on an old one. You can also directly use <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Lean.instantiateTypeLevelParams#doc\">docs#Lean.instantiateTypeLevelParams</a> here to get the type for an instantiation of level parameters but it's more convenient to just <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Lean.Meta.inferType#doc\">docs#Lean.Meta.inferType</a> on a <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Lean.Expr.const#doc\">docs#Lean.Expr.const</a> expression for that purpose.</p>",
        "id": 627435113,
        "sender_full_name": "Robin Arnez",
        "timestamp": 1790601614
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>If you don't know which level parameters you want ahead of time, you might want to use <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Lean.Meta.mkConstWithFreshMVarLevels#doc\">docs#Lean.Meta.mkConstWithFreshMVarLevels</a>. In comparison to the result of <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Lean.getConstVal#doc\">docs#Lean.getConstVal</a>, which at first is only valid if you have precisely the level parameters it has, the result of <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Lean.Meta.mkConstWithFreshMVarLevels#doc\">docs#Lean.Meta.mkConstWithFreshMVarLevels</a> is already valid in context; although you need to be careful to make sure to instantiate the level metavariables eventually</p>",
        "id": 627435947,
        "sender_full_name": "Robin Arnez",
        "timestamp": 1790601788
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Robin, thanks for the very comprehensive answer.  Somehow I had overlooked the fact that I can just build an <code>Expr</code> with the given id directly (e.g. using <code>Lean.mkConst</code>) rather than going through <code>elabTerm</code>!  I think my intuition that <code>elabTerm</code> was too heavyweight was correct.  :)</p>\n<p>The second of your four solutions above is probably adequate for my needs at this time, but I will likely refer to this post again as I delve deeper into these waters.  :)  Thanks again.</p>",
        "id": 627436567,
        "sender_full_name": "Adam Dingle",
        "timestamp": 1790601910
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Actually I think things are not quite so simple, because (as I wrote in my original message) the identifier might be either a local variable or a global constant.  In this situation it appears that I must check for both cases explicitly, e.g. like this:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Lean</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">open</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Lean</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">open</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Lean</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Meta</span>\n\n<span class=\"c1\">-- Return the type of a local variable or global constant.</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">get_type</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Name</span><span class=\"o\">):</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">MetaM</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Expr</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">do</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">e</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">←</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">if</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hasConst</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">then</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">pure</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">$</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Lean</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">mkConst</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">else</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">getFVarFromUserName</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">inferType</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">e</span>\n\n<span class=\"c1\">-- a global constant</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">z</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Int</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">7</span>\n\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">eval</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">do</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"c1\">-- Declare a local variable x : Nat in the current LocalContext.</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">withLocalDecl</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"ss\">`x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">default</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">mkConst</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"ss\">``Nat</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">do</span>\n\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"c1\">-- Look up the types of x and z.</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">pure</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">get_type</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"ss\">`x</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">get_type</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"ss\">`z</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"c1\">-- produces (Lean.Expr.const `Nat [], Lean.Expr.const `Int [])</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>If there is some call I can make to avoid having to check these cases separately, I'd be curious to know about it.  Still, as I've written it this is pretty easy.</p>",
        "id": 627466551,
        "sender_full_name": "Adam Dingle",
        "timestamp": 1790607839
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>A minor note on the snippet you provided: I think that if you have a free variable in the local context with the same name as a global constant, the local free variable should shadow the global constant but your script will return the type of the global constant. I think just switching the order of your checks (and including a try-catch for <code>getFVarFromUserName</code>) would be sufficient to fix that.</p>",
        "id": 627474733,
        "sender_full_name": "Josh Clune",
        "timestamp": 1790609264
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Josh: Excellent point, thanks.  Rather than a try-catch I'd slightly prefer to use a function call, e.g. like this:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">get_type</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Name</span><span class=\"o\">):</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">MetaM</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Expr</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">do</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">e</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">match</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">getLCtx</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">findFromUserName?</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">with</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">some</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">decl</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Expr</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">fvar</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">decl</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">fvarId</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">none</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Lean</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">mkConst</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">inferType</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">e</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 627489032,
        "sender_full_name": "Adam Dingle",
        "timestamp": 1790612412
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Are you sure that the declaration you run this on will not contain level parameters?</p>",
        "id": 627523195,
        "sender_full_name": "Robin Arnez",
        "timestamp": 1790620600
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>because otherwise, you might want use e.g. <code>mkConstWithFreshMVarsLevel n</code> instead of <code>mkConst n</code></p>",
        "id": 627523307,
        "sender_full_name": "Robin Arnez",
        "timestamp": 1790620629
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>or whatever is most reasonable in your case</p>",
        "id": 627523338,
        "sender_full_name": "Robin Arnez",
        "timestamp": 1790620636
    }
]